<%#
  Four frames of a running figure in profile, stacked into one strip. The CSS
  shows six lines at a time and steps the strip up a frame per step; the
  whitespace is load-bearing, so leave the alignment alone.

  The cycle is stride, gather, opposite stride, gather. Feet land on the last
  row of every frame and the head rises a line on the gathered frames, because
  the legs fold under the body rather than the body leaving the ground. Arms
  alternate high and low, which is the cue a front-on figure cannot give.

  Decorative throughout — hidden from assistive technology, and frozen on the
  first frame where motion is not wanted.
%>
<div class="ascii-runner select-none font-mono text-accent <%= local_assigns[:classes] %>"
     aria-hidden="true">
  <pre class="ascii-runner__frames">       o
       |_/
     \_|
      / \
     /   \
    /    |

       o
     \_|
       |_/
       |\
       |
       o
     \_|
       |_/
      / \
     /   \
     |    \

       o
       |_/
     \_|
      /|
       |
</pre>
</div>
